{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e4f2899699eef75a","name":"Q7-Series Astromech Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-e4f2899699eef75a","title":"Q7-Series Astromech Droid","revision":19548,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:10:19Z","sha256":"c62f6698bc3723cbd57010bbabd8d4fb3377c319f19095a2b505b543d3fc21e7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19548","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Q7-Series%20Astromech%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e4f2899699eef75a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed specifically to tie in to the systems of the Alpha-3 ",{"tag":"a","children":["V-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/V-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:40377b32dd9b36ce"},", the Q7-Series of Astromech Droids was an experiment for its manufacturer, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Industrial Automaton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Industrial_Automaton","referenceId":"reference:8ab52c937ff3814a"},". Unlike the previous models of Astromech, the Q7 moved by means of a repulsorlift. Although ",{"tag":"a","children":["Industrial Automaton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Industrial_Automaton","referenceId":"reference:8ab52c937ff3814a"}," had used repulsorlift designs for simple devices such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Holocam Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Holocam_Droids"}," and training remotes, it had never before attempted to make anything as multipurpose as an Astromech with a hover capacity. Indeed, the company's efforts to give R2 models even limited flight ability with aftermarket leg-jets resulted in devices that broke down more often than they worked, forcing the manufacturer to stop supporting the flight accessories.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, the design of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["V-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/V-Wing"}," required an Astromech that took up little space and could get itself in and out of its work socket. A repulsor Hoverdroid seemed the best answer, and IA felt the lucrative military contracts that a successful design would bring was worth the risk. After numerous prototypes (designated Q1 through Q6), a working blueprint was achieved. IA based the Q7 on the upper dome of its popular R2-Series, both to save costs on retooling parts and because the R2s were well loved throughout the galaxy. Rather than a large cylindrical body, however, the Q7 had a lower dome as well, making it a hovering sphere less than a meter in diameter.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For a few years the Q7 seemed destined to replace the R2 as the company's greatest success. The smaller hovering Droids were just as smart and adaptable as their bigger cousins (largely because of very similar core programming), and they had the same plucky, fearless personality that allowed them to operate in combat conditions. However, problems turned up. The repulsorlift broke down more often than tracks, cost more to repair, and had no backup system to allow locomotion when it failed. The Q7 had much less interior room, leaving it only a few standard tool and manipulator options. And finally, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["V-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/V-Wing"}," was replaced by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},", and new Imperial military planners felt no need for Astromechs in their fighter craft.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Production was stopped, and the remaining stock of Q7s was sold at large discounts. In the decades right after ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", this made them a common sight with smugglers and Outer Rim merchants. By the time of the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},", the high cost of maintaining the hovering Astromechs had convinced most owners to give up on them. Many were converted to R2- or R4-like tracked Droids, and others had their memories transferred to entirely different models. Although a few might still be encountered as oddities, the era of the Q7 was over.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Q7-Series Astromech Droids can by played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Q7-Series Astromech Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 2 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag